  "id": "skyridge-booster-box",
  "name": "Skyridge booster box",
  "category": "product_promotion",
  "description": {
    "text": "Sealed Skyridge booster boxes, from 12 May 2003, each came with one oversized box topper, a jumbo copy of one of four of the set's secret rare Crystal cards: Charizard, Crobat, Ho-Oh or Kabutops. They are 9/12 to 12/12, the last of the twelve box toppers of Wizards of the Coast's e-Card series, and Skyridge was the last set Wizards made. Unlike the cardboard toppers of Expedition and Aquapolis, these are printed on clear, see-through plastic.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Flipside Gaming: Retrospective, Skyridge (2017)",
        "url": "https://flipsidegaming.com/blogs/pokemon-blog/retrospective-skyridge"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: the e-Card box toppers and the clear plastic Skyridge cards",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/does-anyone-remember-the-clear-plastic-cards/10584"
      },
      {
        "title": "Elite Fourum: Skyridge box toppers",
        "url": "https://www.elitefourum.com/t/skyridge-box-toppers/23327"
      },
      {
        "title": "Bulbapedia: Box Topper (TCG) (Wayback Machine copy, 27 July 2026)",
        "url": "https://web.archive.org/web/20260727023621/https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Box_Topper_(TCG)"
      }
    ]
  },
